x86_64-windows the one name that differs is `anon` in the `inline namespace { }`: the Microsoft ABI names an unnamed namespace `?A0x<hash>@`, a hash of the translation unit that clang-cl and cl each answer differently, where cxx1 writes `_GLOBAL__N_1` - the same recorded difference as namespace-unnamed.nonames, and nothing to do with the inline mark. The other six names agree, as do all seven on both Itanium targets.